%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 903032e1824c5e342aea2c5d148d5f3c, type: 3}
  m_Name: EndingStoryDatabase
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::EndingStoryDatabase
  saveId: MainEndingStoryDatabase
  endings:
  - endingId: collapse
    title: Trust Collapse
    story: The trust crisis becomes impossible to control. Even when you post the
      truth, nobody believes you anymore. Sponsors leave, followers attack each other,
      and your name becomes a warning about what happens when misinformation destroys
      credibility.
  - endingId: forgotten
    title: Forgotten
    story: Your account slowly disappears into the endless feed. You did not make
      enough money, did not build trust, and did not keep an audience. In the end,
      your posts remain online, but almost nobody remembers them.
  - endingId: noise_empire
    title: Noise Empire
    story: You built a massive platform through outrage, fear, and misinformation.
      Money poured in, followers multiplied, and your posts dominated every feed.
      But the empire stands on a broken foundation. People watch you, but they no
      longer trust you.
  - endingId: viral_beast
    title: Viral Beast
    story: Your content spreads faster than you can control. Millions of people see
      your posts, but many of them follow you for chaos, not trust. You became famous,
      but the audience you created is angry, unstable, and hard to stop.
  - endingId: quiet_cash
    title: Quiet Cash
    story: You did not become widely famous, but you found a way to make money quietly.
      Sponsors and private deals kept you alive, even without a huge audience. Your
      influence is small, but financially, you survived.
  - endingId: broke_star
    title: Broke Star
    story: People like you, share your posts, and recognize your name, but popularity
      does not pay the bills. You built an audience, but failed to turn attention
      into money. Your influence is real, but your future is financially uncertain.
  - endingId: powerhouse
    title: Powerhouse
    story: 'You achieved the rarest result: money, trust, and influence at the same
      time. Your content reaches a large audience without relying on manipulation.
      People follow you because they believe you, and your platform becomes both
      successful and respected.'
  - endingId: trusted
    title: Trusted
    story: You became a voice people rely on. Your audience grew because your content
      felt responsible, careful, and believable. You may not control the whole media
      landscape, but when people need clarity, they come to you.
  - endingId: honest_path
    title: Honest Path
    story: You refused to chase easy lies. Your growth was slower, and money remained
      a problem, but people trusted you. You did not become rich, but you protected
      your integrity.
  - endingId: balanced
    title: Responsible Influencer
    story: You found a stable balance between income, influence, and responsibility.
      You made mistakes, but you corrected them before they became disasters. Your
      platform survives because people see you as imperfect, but mostly trustworthy.
  - endingId: paid_lies
    title: Paid Lies
    story: You learned that misinformation can be profitable. Sponsors, clicks, and
      ads rewarded your worst choices. You end the month with money, but your reputation
      is permanently damaged.
  - endingId: mixed_legacy
    title: Unclear Legacy
    story: Your month ends with a mixed record. You gained some attention, lost some
      trust, made some money, and left behind arguments that people still debate.
      Some remember you as entertaining. Others remember the damage. Your legacy
      depends on who tells the story.
